# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "A free IBM course on quantum information and computation"
msgstr "Un cours IBM gratuit sur l'information et le calcul quantiques"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Analysis"
msgstr "Analyse"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now we'll analyze Grover's algorithm to understand how it works.\n"
"We'll start with what could be described as a *symbolic* analysis, where we calculate how the Grover operation $G$ acts on certain states, and then we'll tie this symbolic analysis to a *geometric* picture that's helpful for visualizing how the algorithm works.\n"
msgstr ""
"Nous allons maintenant analyser l'algorithme de Grover pour comprendre son fonctionnement.\n"
"Nous commencerons par ce qu'on pourrait appeler une analyse *symbolique*, où nous calculons comment l'opération de Grover $G$ agit sur certains états, puis nous relierons cette analyse symbolique à une représentation *géométrique* qui aide à visualiser le fonctionnement de l'algorithme.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Solutions and non-solutions {#solutions-and-non-solutions}"
msgstr "Solutions et non-solutions {#solutions-and-non-solutions}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let's start by defining two sets of strings.\n"
msgstr "Commençons par définir deux ensembles de chaînes.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  A_0 &= \\bigl\\{ x\\in\\Sigma^n : f(x) = 0\\bigr\\} \\\\\n"
"  A_1 &= \\bigl\\{ x\\in\\Sigma^n : f(x) = 1\\bigr\\}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  A_0 &= \\bigl\\{ x\\in\\Sigma^n : f(x) = 0\\bigr\\} \\\\\n"
"  A_1 &= \\bigl\\{ x\\in\\Sigma^n : f(x) = 1\\bigr\\}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The set $A_1$ contains all of the solutions to our search problem while $A_0$ contains the strings that aren't solutions (which we can refer to as *non-solutions* when it's convenient).\n"
"These two sets satisfy $A_0 \\cap A_1 = \\varnothing$ and $A_0 \\cup A_1 = \\Sigma^n$, which is to say that this is a *bipartition* of $\\Sigma^n$.\n"
msgstr ""
"L'ensemble $A_1$ contient toutes les solutions à notre problème de recherche, tandis que $A_0$ contient les chaînes qui ne sont pas des solutions (qu'on peut appeler *non-solutions* quand c'est pratique).\n"
"Ces deux ensembles vérifient $A_0 \\cap A_1 = \\varnothing$ et $A_0 \\cup A_1 = \\Sigma^n$, c'est-à-dire qu'il s'agit d'une *bipartition* de $\\Sigma^n$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next we'll define two unit vectors representing uniform superpositions over the sets of solutions and non-solutions.\n"
msgstr "Ensuite, nous allons définir deux vecteurs unitaires représentant des superpositions uniformes sur les ensembles de solutions et de non-solutions.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert A_0\\rangle &= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\vert A_0\\vert}} \\sum_{x\\in A_0} \\vert x\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  \\vert A_1\\rangle &= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\vert A_1\\vert}} \\sum_{x\\in A_1} \\vert x\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert A_0\\rangle &= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\vert A_0\\vert}} \\sum_{x\\in A_0} \\vert x\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  \\vert A_1\\rangle &= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\vert A_1\\vert}} \\sum_{x\\in A_1} \\vert x\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Formally speaking, each of these vectors is only defined when its corresponding set is nonempty, but hereafter we're going to focus on the case that neither $A_0$ nor $A_1$ is empty.\n"
"The cases that $A_0 = \\varnothing$ and $A_1 = \\varnothing$ are easily handled separately, and we'll do that later.\n"
msgstr ""
"Formellement, chacun de ces vecteurs n'est défini que lorsque l'ensemble correspondant est non vide, mais nous allons désormais nous concentrer sur le cas où ni $A_0$ ni $A_1$ n'est vide.\n"
"Les cas $A_0 = \\varnothing$ et $A_1 = \\varnothing$ se traitent facilement séparément, et nous le ferons plus tard.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As an aside, the notation being used here is common: any time we have a finite and nonempty set $S$, we can write $\\vert S\\rangle$ to denote the quantum state vector that's uniform over the elements of $S$.\n"
msgstr "En passant, la notation utilisée ici est courante : chaque fois que nous avons un ensemble fini et non vide $S$, on peut écrire $\\vert S\\rangle$ pour désigner le vecteur d'état quantique uniforme sur les éléments de $S$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let's also define $\\vert u \\rangle$ to be a *uniform* quantum state over all $n$-bit strings:\n"
msgstr "Définissons également $\\vert u \\rangle$ comme l'état quantique *uniforme* sur toutes les chaînes de $n$ bits :\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert u\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{N}} \\sum_{x\\in\\Sigma^n} \\vert x\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert u\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{N}} \\sum_{x\\in\\Sigma^n} \\vert x\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Notice that\n"
msgstr "Remarque :\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert u\\rangle\n"
"= \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0 \\vert}{N}} \\vert A_0\\rangle\n"
"+ \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1 \\vert}{N}} \\vert A_1\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert u\\rangle\n"
"= \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0 \\vert}{N}} \\vert A_0\\rangle\n"
"+ \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1 \\vert}{N}} \\vert A_1\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We also have that $\\vert u\\rangle = H^{\\otimes n} \\vert 0^n \\rangle$, so $\\vert u\\rangle$ represents the state of the register $\\mathsf{Q}$ after the initialization in step 1 of Grover's algorithm.\n"
msgstr "On a aussi $\\vert u\\rangle = H^{\\otimes n} \\vert 0^n \\rangle$, donc $\\vert u\\rangle$ représente l'état du registre $\\mathsf{Q}$ après l'initialisation à l'étape 1 de l'algorithme de Grover.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This implies that just before the iterations of $G$ happen in step 2, the state of $\\mathsf{Q}$ is contained in the two-dimensional vector space spanned by $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ and $\\vert A_1\\rangle$, and moreover the coefficients of these vectors are real numbers.\n"
"As we will see, the state of $\\mathsf{Q}$ will always have these properties — meaning that the state is a real linear combination of $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ and $\\vert A_1\\rangle$ — after any number of iterations of the operation $G$ in step 2.\n"
msgstr ""
"Cela implique que juste avant les itérations de $G$ à l'étape 2, l'état de $\\mathsf{Q}$ est contenu dans l'espace vectoriel bidimensionnel engendré par $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ et $\\vert A_1\\rangle$, et de plus les coefficients de ces vecteurs sont des nombres réels.\n"
"Comme nous le verrons, l'état de $\\mathsf{Q}$ aura toujours ces propriétés — c'est-à-dire que l'état est une combinaison linéaire réelle de $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ et $\\vert A_1\\rangle$ — après n'importe quel nombre d'itérations de l'opération $G$ à l'étape 2.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "An observation about the Grover operation {#an-observation-about-the-grover-operation}"
msgstr "Une observation sur l'opération de Grover {#an-observation-about-the-grover-operation}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We'll now turn our attention to the Grover operation\n"
msgstr "Intéressons-nous maintenant à l'opération de Grover\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"G = H^{\\otimes n} Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} H^{\\otimes n} Z_f,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"G = H^{\\otimes n} Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} H^{\\otimes n} Z_f,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "beginning with an interesting observation about it.\n"
msgstr "en commençant par une observation intéressante à son sujet.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Imagine for a moment that we replaced the function $f$ by the composition of $f$ with the NOT function — or, in other words, the function we get by flipping the output bit of $f$.\n"
"We'll call this new function $g$, and we can express it using symbols in a few alternative ways.\n"
msgstr ""
"Imagine un instant que nous remplaçions la fonction $f$ par la composition de $f$ avec la fonction NOT — autrement dit, la fonction obtenue en inversant le bit de sortie de $f$.\n"
"Appelons cette nouvelle fonction $g$ ; on peut l'exprimer de plusieurs manières équivalentes.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"g(x) = \\neg f(x) = 1 \\oplus f(x) = 1 - f(x) =\n"
"\\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & f(x) = 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & f(x) = 1\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"g(x) = \\neg f(x) = 1 \\oplus f(x) = 1 - f(x) =\n"
"\\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & f(x) = 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & f(x) = 1\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"(-1)^{g(x)} = (-1)^{1 \\oplus f(x)} = - (-1)^{f(x)}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"(-1)^{g(x)} = (-1)^{1 \\oplus f(x)} = - (-1)^{f(x)}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "for every string $x\\in\\Sigma^n$, and therefore\n"
msgstr "pour toute chaîne $x\\in\\Sigma^n$, et donc\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"Z_g = - Z_f.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"Z_g = - Z_f.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This means that if we were to substitute the function $f$ with the function $g$, Grover's algorithm wouldn't function any differently — because the states we obtain from the algorithm in the two cases are necessarily equivalent up to a global phase.\n"
msgstr "Cela signifie que si on substituait la fonction $f$ par la fonction $g$, l'algorithme de Grover ne fonctionnerait pas différemment — car les états obtenus par l'algorithme dans les deux cas sont nécessairement équivalents à une phase globale près.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This isn't a problem!\n"
"Intuitively speaking, the algorithm doesn't care which strings are solutions and which are non-solutions — it only needs to be able to *distinguish* solutions and non-solutions to operate correctly.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ce n'est pas un problème !\n"
"Intuitivement, l'algorithme n'a pas à savoir quelles chaînes sont des solutions et lesquelles sont des non-solutions — il lui suffit de pouvoir *distinguer* solutions et non-solutions pour fonctionner correctement.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Action of the Grover operation {#action-of-the-grover-operation}"
msgstr "Action de l'opération de Grover {#action-of-the-grover-operation}"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now let's consider the action of $G$ on the quantum state vectors $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ and $\\vert A_1\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr "Considérons maintenant l'action de $G$ sur les vecteurs d'état quantique $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ et $\\vert A_1\\rangle$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "First, let's observe that the operation $Z_f$ has a very simple action on $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ and $\\vert A_1\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr "D'abord, observons que l'opération $Z_f$ a une action très simple sur $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ et $\\vert A_1\\rangle$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"Z_f \\vert A_0\\rangle & = \\vert A_0\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"Z_f \\vert A_1\\rangle & = -\\vert A_1\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"Z_f \\vert A_0\\rangle & = \\vert A_0\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"Z_f \\vert A_1\\rangle & = -\\vert A_1\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Second, we have the operation $H^{\\otimes n} Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} H^{\\otimes n}$.\n"
"The operation $Z_{\\mathrm{OR}}$ is defined as\n"
msgstr ""
"Ensuite, considérons l'opération $H^{\\otimes n} Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} H^{\\otimes n}$.\n"
"L'opération $Z_{\\mathrm{OR}}$ est définie par\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} \\vert x\\rangle\n"
"= \\begin{cases}\n"
"\\vert x\\rangle & x = 0^n \\\\[2mm]\n"
"-\\vert x\\rangle & x \\neq 0^n,\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} \\vert x\\rangle\n"
"= \\begin{cases}\n"
"\\vert x\\rangle & x = 0^n \\\\[2mm]\n"
"-\\vert x\\rangle & x \\neq 0^n,\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "again for every string $x\\in\\Sigma^n$, and a convenient alternative way to express this operation is like this:\n"
msgstr "de nouveau pour toute chaîne $x\\in\\Sigma^n$, et une façon alternative commode d'exprimer cette opération est la suivante :\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} = 2 \\vert 0^n \\rangle \\langle 0^n \\vert - \\mathbb{I}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} = 2 \\vert 0^n \\rangle \\langle 0^n \\vert - \\mathbb{I}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A simple way to verify that this expression agrees with the definition of $Z_{\\mathrm{OR}}$ is to evaluate its action on standard basis states.\n"
msgstr "Une façon simple de vérifier que cette expression est bien conforme à la définition de $Z_{\\mathrm{OR}}$ est d'évaluer son action sur les états de la base standard.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The operation $H^{\\otimes n} Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} H^{\\otimes n}$ can therefore be written like this:\n"
msgstr "L'opération $H^{\\otimes n} Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} H^{\\otimes n}$ peut donc s'écrire ainsi :\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H^{\\otimes n} Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} H^{\\otimes n} = 2 H^{\\otimes n} \\vert 0^n \\rangle \\langle 0^n \\vert H^{\\otimes n} - \\mathbb{I} = 2 \\vert u \\rangle \\langle u \\vert - \\mathbb{I},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H^{\\otimes n} Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} H^{\\otimes n} = 2 H^{\\otimes n} \\vert 0^n \\rangle \\langle 0^n \\vert H^{\\otimes n} - \\mathbb{I} = 2 \\vert u \\rangle \\langle u \\vert - \\mathbb{I},\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "using the same notation, $\\vert u \\rangle$, that we used above for the uniform superposition over all $n$-bit strings.\n"
msgstr "en utilisant la même notation, $\\vert u \\rangle,$ que celle utilisée plus haut pour la superposition uniforme sur toutes les chaînes de $n$ bits.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"And now we have what we need to compute the action of $G$ on $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ and $\\vert A_1\\rangle$.\n"
"First let's compute the action of $G$ on $\\vert A_0\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Nous avons maintenant tout ce qu'il faut pour calculer l'action de $G$ sur $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ et $\\vert A_1\\rangle$.\n"
"Calculons d'abord l'action de $G$ sur $\\vert A_0\\rangle$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  G \\vert A_0 \\rangle\n"
"  & = \\bigl( 2 \\vert u\\rangle \\langle u \\vert - \\mathbb{I}\\bigr) Z_f \\vert A_0\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = \\bigl( 2 \\vert u\\rangle \\langle u \\vert - \\mathbb{I}\\bigr) \\vert A_0\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = 2 \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}} \\vert u\\rangle -\\vert A_0 \\rangle\\\\\n"
"  & = 2 \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}} \\biggl(\n"
"  \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}} \\vert A_0\\rangle + \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} \\vert A_1\\rangle\\biggr)\n"
"  -\\vert A_0 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = \\biggl( \\frac{2\\vert A_0\\vert}{N} - 1\\biggr) \\vert A_0 \\rangle\n"
"  + \\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_0\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_1\\vert}}{N} \\vert A_1 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = \\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert - \\vert A_1\\vert}{N} \\vert A_0 \\rangle\n"
"  + \\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_0\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_1\\vert}}{N} \\vert A_1 \\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  G \\vert A_0 \\rangle\n"
"  & = \\bigl( 2 \\vert u\\rangle \\langle u \\vert - \\mathbb{I}\\bigr) Z_f \\vert A_0\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = \\bigl( 2 \\vert u\\rangle \\langle u \\vert - \\mathbb{I}\\bigr) \\vert A_0\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = 2 \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}} \\vert u\\rangle -\\vert A_0 \\rangle\\\\\n"
"  & = 2 \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}} \\biggl(\n"
"  \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}} \\vert A_0\\rangle + \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} \\vert A_1\\rangle\\biggr)\n"
"  -\\vert A_0 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = \\biggl( \\frac{2\\vert A_0\\vert}{N} - 1\\biggr) \\vert A_0 \\rangle\n"
"  + \\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_0\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_1\\vert}}{N} \\vert A_1 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = \\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert - \\vert A_1\\vert}{N} \\vert A_0 \\rangle\n"
"  + \\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_0\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_1\\vert}}{N} \\vert A_1 \\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "And second, let's compute the action of $G$ on $\\vert A_1\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr "Puis calculons l'action de $G$ sur $\\vert A_1\\rangle$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  G \\vert A_1 \\rangle\n"
"  & = \\bigl( 2 \\vert u\\rangle \\langle u \\vert - \\mathbb{I} \\bigr) Z_f \\vert A_1\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = - \\bigl( 2 \\vert u\\rangle \\langle u \\vert - \\mathbb{I} \\bigr) \\vert A_1\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = - 2 \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} \\vert u\\rangle + \\vert A_1 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = - 2 \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} \\biggl(\\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}} \\vert A_0\\rangle\n"
"      + \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} \\vert A_1\\rangle\\biggr) + \\vert A_1 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = - \\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_1\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_0\\vert}}{N} \\vert A_0 \\rangle\n"
"      + \\biggl( 1 - \\frac{2\\vert A_1\\vert}{N} \\biggr) \\vert A_1 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = - \\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_1\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_0\\vert}}{N} \\vert A_0 \\rangle\n"
"      + \\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert - \\vert A_1\\vert}{N} \\vert A_1 \\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  G \\vert A_1 \\rangle\n"
"  & = \\bigl( 2 \\vert u\\rangle \\langle u \\vert - \\mathbb{I} \\bigr) Z_f \\vert A_1\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = - \\bigl( 2 \\vert u\\rangle \\langle u \\vert - \\mathbb{I} \\bigr) \\vert A_1\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = - 2 \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} \\vert u\\rangle + \\vert A_1 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = - 2 \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} \\biggl(\\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}} \\vert A_0\\rangle\n"
"      + \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} \\vert A_1\\rangle\\biggr) + \\vert A_1 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = - \\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_1\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_0\\vert}}{N} \\vert A_0 \\rangle\n"
"      + \\biggl( 1 - \\frac{2\\vert A_1\\vert}{N} \\biggr) \\vert A_1 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = - \\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_1\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_0\\vert}}{N} \\vert A_0 \\rangle\n"
"      + \\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert - \\vert A_1\\vert}{N} \\vert A_1 \\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In both cases we're using the equation\n"
msgstr "Dans les deux cas, nous utilisons l'équation\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert u\\rangle\n"
"= \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0 \\vert}{N}} \\vert A_0\\rangle\n"
"+ \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1 \\vert}{N}} \\vert A_1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert u\\rangle\n"
"= \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0 \\vert}{N}} \\vert A_0\\rangle\n"
"+ \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1 \\vert}{N}} \\vert A_1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "along with the expressions\n"
msgstr "ainsi que les expressions\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle u \\vert A_0\\rangle = \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0 \\vert}{N}}\n"
"\\qquad\\text{and}\\qquad\n"
"\\langle u \\vert A_1\\rangle = \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1 \\vert}{N}}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle u \\vert A_0\\rangle = \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0 \\vert}{N}}\n"
"\\qquad\\text{et}\\qquad\n"
"\\langle u \\vert A_1\\rangle = \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1 \\vert}{N}}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "that follow.\n"
msgstr "qui en découlent.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In summary, we have\n"
msgstr "En résumé, nous avons\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  G \\vert A_0 \\rangle\n"
"  & = \\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert - \\vert A_1\\vert}{N} \\vert A_0 \\rangle\n"
"  + \\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_0\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_1\\vert}}{N} \\vert A_1 \\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  G \\vert A_1 \\rangle\n"
"  & = - \\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_1\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_0\\vert}}{N} \\vert A_0 \\rangle\n"
"      + \\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert - \\vert A_1\\vert}{N} \\vert A_1 \\rangle.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  G \\vert A_0 \\rangle\n"
"  & = \\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert - \\vert A_1\\vert}{N} \\vert A_0 \\rangle\n"
"  + \\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_0\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_1\\vert}}{N} \\vert A_1 \\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  G \\vert A_1 \\rangle\n"
"  & = - \\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_1\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_0\\vert}}{N} \\vert A_0 \\rangle\n"
"      + \\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert - \\vert A_1\\vert}{N} \\vert A_1 \\rangle.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As we already noted, the state of $\\mathsf{Q}$ just prior to step 2 is contained in the two-dimensional space spanned by $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ and $\\vert A_1\\rangle$, and we have just established that $G$ maps any vector in this space to another vector in the same space.\n"
"This means that, for the sake of the analysis, we can focus our attention exclusively on this subspace.\n"
msgstr ""
"Comme nous l'avons déjà noté, l'état de $\\mathsf{Q}$ juste avant l'étape 2 est contenu dans l'espace bidimensionnel engendré par $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ et $\\vert A_1\\rangle$, et nous venons d'établir que $G$ envoie tout vecteur de cet espace sur un autre vecteur du même espace.\n"
"Cela signifie que, pour les besoins de l'analyse, nous pouvons concentrer notre attention exclusivement sur ce sous-espace.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To better understand what's happening within this two-dimensional space, let's express the action of $G$ on this space as a matrix,\n"
msgstr "Pour mieux comprendre ce qui se passe dans cet espace bidimensionnel, exprimons l'action de $G$ sur cet espace sous forme de matrice,\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"M = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert - \\vert A_1\\vert}{N} & -\\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_1\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_0\\vert}}{N} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_0\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_1\\vert}}{N} & \\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert - \\vert A_1\\vert}{N}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"M = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert - \\vert A_1\\vert}{N} & -\\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_1\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_0\\vert}}{N} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_0\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_1\\vert}}{N} & \\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert - \\vert A_1\\vert}{N}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"whose first and second rows/columns correspond to $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ and $\\vert A_1\\rangle$, respectively.\n"
"So far in this series, we've always connected the rows and columns of matrices with the classical states of a system, but matrices can also be used to describe the actions of linear mappings on different bases like we have here.\n"
msgstr ""
"dont les première et deuxième lignes/colonnes correspondent respectivement à $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ et $\\vert A_1\\rangle$.\n"
"Jusqu'ici dans cette série, nous avons toujours associé les lignes et colonnes des matrices aux états classiques d'un système, mais les matrices peuvent aussi servir à décrire l'action de transformations linéaires sur différentes bases, comme c'est le cas ici.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "While it isn't at all obvious at first glance, the matrix $M$ is what we obtain by *squaring* a simpler-looking matrix.\n"
msgstr "Bien que ce ne soit pas du tout évident au premier coup d'œil, la matrice $M$ est ce qu'on obtient en *élevant au carré* une matrice d'apparence plus simple.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}} & - \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} & \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}^2\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}} & - \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} & \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}^2\n"
"=\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert - \\vert A_1\\vert}{N} & -\\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_1\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_0\\vert}}{N} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_0\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_1\\vert}}{N} & \\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert - \\vert A_1\\vert}{N}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} = M\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert - \\vert A_1\\vert}{N} & -\\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_1\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_0\\vert}}{N} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_0\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_1\\vert}}{N} & \\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert - \\vert A_1\\vert}{N}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} = M\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The matrix\n"
msgstr "La matrice\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}} & - \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} & \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}} & - \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} & \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "is a *rotation matrix*, which we can alternatively express as\n"
msgstr "est une *matrice de rotation*, qu'on peut également écrire sous la forme\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}} & - \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} & \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}} & - \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} & \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\cos(\\theta) & -\\sin(\\theta) \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\sin(\\theta) & \\cos(\\theta)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\cos(\\theta) & -\\sin(\\theta) \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\sin(\\theta) & \\cos(\\theta)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "for\n"
msgstr "pour\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\theta = \\sin^{-1}\\biggl(\\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}}\\biggr).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\theta = \\sin^{-1}\\biggl(\\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}}\\biggr).\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This angle $\\theta$ is going to play a very important role in the analysis that follows, so it's worth stressing its importance here as we see it for the first time.\n"
msgstr "Cet angle $\\theta$ va jouer un rôle très important dans l'analyse qui suit, aussi vaut-il la peine d'insister sur son importance dès sa première apparition.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In light of this expression of this matrix, we observe that\n"
msgstr "À la lumière de cette expression, nous observons que\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"M = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\cos(\\theta) & -\\sin(\\theta) \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\sin(\\theta) & \\cos(\\theta)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}^2\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\cos(2\\theta) & -\\sin(2\\theta) \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\sin(2\\theta) & \\cos(2\\theta)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"M = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\cos(\\theta) & -\\sin(\\theta) \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\sin(\\theta) & \\cos(\\theta)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}^2\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\cos(2\\theta) & -\\sin(2\\theta) \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\sin(2\\theta) & \\cos(2\\theta)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is because rotating by the angle $\\theta$ two times is equivalent to rotating by the angle $2\\theta$.\n"
"Another way to see this is to make use of the alternative expression\n"
msgstr ""
"C'est parce qu'effectuer deux rotations d'angle $\\theta$ revient à effectuer une rotation d'angle $2\\theta$.\n"
"Une autre façon de le voir est d'utiliser l'expression alternative\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\theta\n"
"= \\cos^{-1}\\biggl(\\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}}\\biggr),\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\theta\n"
"= \\cos^{-1}\\biggl(\\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}}\\biggr),\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "together with the *double angle* formulas from trigonometry:\n"
msgstr "avec les formules de *duplication* issues de la trigonométrie :\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\cos(2\\theta) & = \\cos^2(\\theta) - \\sin^2(\\theta)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\sin(2\\theta) & = 2 \\sin(\\theta)\\cos(\\theta).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
"In summary, the state of the register $\\mathsf{Q}$ at the start of step 2 is\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\cos(2\\theta) & = \\cos^2(\\theta) - \\sin^2(\\theta)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\sin(2\\theta) & = 2 \\sin(\\theta)\\cos(\\theta).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert u\\rangle\n"
"= \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}} \\vert A_0\\rangle\n"
"+ \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} \\vert A_1\\rangle\n"
"= \\cos(\\theta) \\vert A_0\\rangle + \\sin(\\theta) \\vert A_1\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert u\\rangle\n"
"= \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}} \\vert A_0\\rangle\n"
"+ \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} \\vert A_1\\rangle\n"
"= \\cos(\\theta) \\vert A_0\\rangle + \\sin(\\theta) \\vert A_1\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"and the effect of applying $G$ to this state is to rotate it by an angle $2\\theta$ within the space spanned by $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ and $\\vert A_1\\rangle$.\n"
"So, for example, we have\n"
msgstr ""
"et l'effet d'appliquer $G$ sur cet état est de le faire tourner d'un angle $2\\theta$ dans l'espace engendré par $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ et $\\vert A_1\\rangle$.\n"
"Donc, par exemple, nous avons\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"G \\vert u \\rangle &= \\cos(3\\theta) \\vert A_0\\rangle + \\sin(3\\theta) \\vert A_1\\rangle\\\\[1mm]\n"
"G^2 \\vert u \\rangle &= \\cos(5\\theta) \\vert A_0\\rangle + \\sin(5\\theta) \\vert A_1\\rangle\\\\[1mm]\n"
"G^3 \\vert u \\rangle &= \\cos(7\\theta) \\vert A_0\\rangle + \\sin(7\\theta) \\vert A_1\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"G \\vert u \\rangle &= \\cos(3\\theta) \\vert A_0\\rangle + \\sin(3\\theta) \\vert A_1\\rangle\\\\[1mm]\n"
"G^2 \\vert u \\rangle &= \\cos(5\\theta) \\vert A_0\\rangle + \\sin(5\\theta) \\vert A_1\\rangle\\\\[1mm]\n"
"G^3 \\vert u \\rangle &= \\cos(7\\theta) \\vert A_0\\rangle + \\sin(7\\theta) \\vert A_1\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "and in general\n"
msgstr "et en général\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"G^t \\vert u \\rangle\n"
"= \\cos\\bigl((2t + 1)\\theta\\bigr) \\vert A_0\\rangle\n"
"+ \\sin\\bigl((2t + 1)\\theta\\bigr) \\vert A_1\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"G^t \\vert u \\rangle\n"
"= \\cos\\bigl((2t + 1)\\theta\\bigr) \\vert A_0\\rangle\n"
"+ \\sin\\bigl((2t + 1)\\theta\\bigr) \\vert A_1\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Geometric picture {#geometric-picture}"
msgstr "Représentation géométrique {#geometric-picture}"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now let's connect the analysis we just went through to a geometric picture.\n"
"The idea is that the operation $G$ is the product of two *reflections*,\n"
"$Z_f$ and $H^{\\otimes n} Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} H^{\\otimes n}$.\n"
"And the net effect of performing two reflections is to perform a *rotation*.\n"
msgstr ""
"Relions maintenant l'analyse que nous venons de mener à une représentation géométrique.\n"
"L'idée est que l'opération $G$ est le produit de deux *réflexions*,\n"
"$Z_f$ et $H^{\\otimes n} Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} H^{\\otimes n}.$\n"
"Et l'effet net de deux réflexions est d'effectuer une *rotation*.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let's start with $Z_f$.\n"
"As we already observed previously, we have\n"
msgstr ""
"Commençons par $Z_f$.\n"
"Comme nous l'avons déjà observé précédemment :\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"Z_f \\vert A_0\\rangle & = \\vert A_0\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"Z_f \\vert A_1\\rangle & = -\\vert A_1\\rangle.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"Z_f \\vert A_0\\rangle & = \\vert A_0\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"Z_f \\vert A_1\\rangle & = -\\vert A_1\\rangle.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Within the two-dimensional vector space spanned by $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ and $\\vert A_1\\rangle$,\n"
"this is a *reflection* about the line parallel to $\\vert A_0\\rangle$, which we'll call $L_1$.\n"
"Here's a figure illustrating the action of this reflection on a hypothetical unit vector $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$,\n"
"which we're assuming is a real linear combination of $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ and $\\vert A_1\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dans l'espace vectoriel bidimensionnel engendré par $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ et $\\vert A_1\\rangle$,\n"
"il s'agit d'une *réflexion* par rapport à la droite parallèle à $\\vert A_0\\rangle$, que nous appellerons $L_1$.\n"
"Voici une figure illustrant l'action de cette réflexion sur un vecteur unitaire hypothétique $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$,\n"
"que nous supposons être une combinaison linéaire réelle de $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ et $\\vert A_1\\rangle$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A figure depicting the action of a reflection on a vector.](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/grover-algorithm/reflection1.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Une figure illustrant l'action d'une réflexion sur un vecteur.](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/grover-algorithm/reflection1.svg)\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Second we have the operation $H^{\\otimes n} Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} H^{\\otimes n}$, which we've already seen can be written as\n"
msgstr "Ensuite, nous avons l'opération $H^{\\otimes n} Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} H^{\\otimes n}$, dont nous avons déjà vu qu'elle peut s'écrire\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H^{\\otimes n} Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} H^{\\otimes n} = 2 \\vert u \\rangle \\langle u \\vert - \\mathbb{I}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H^{\\otimes n} Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} H^{\\otimes n} = 2 \\vert u \\rangle \\langle u \\vert - \\mathbb{I}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is also a reflection, this time about the line $L_2$ parallel to the vector $\\vert u\\rangle$.\n"
"Here's a figure depicting the action of this reflection on a unit vector $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Il s'agit également d'une réflexion, cette fois par rapport à la droite $L_2$ parallèle au vecteur $\\vert u\\rangle$.\n"
"Voici une figure représentant l'action de cette réflexion sur un vecteur unitaire $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A figure depicting the action of a second reflection on a vector.](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/grover-algorithm/reflection2.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Une figure illustrant l'action d'une deuxième réflexion sur un vecteur.](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/grover-algorithm/reflection2.svg)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When we compose these two reflections, we obtain a rotation — by twice the angle between the lines of reflection — as this figure illustrates.\n"
msgstr "Lorsque nous composons ces deux réflexions, nous obtenons une rotation — d'un angle égal au double de l'angle entre les axes de réflexion — comme l'illustre cette figure.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A figure depicting the action of the Grover operation on a vector.](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/grover-algorithm/Grover_rotation.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Une figure illustrant l'action de l'opération de Grover sur un vecteur.](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/grover-algorithm/Grover_rotation.svg)\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This explains, in geometric terms, why the effect of the Grover operation is to rotate linear combinations of $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ and $\\vert A_1\\rangle$ by an angle of $2\\theta$.\n"
msgstr "Cela explique, en termes géométriques, pourquoi l'effet de l'opération de Grover est de faire tourner les combinaisons linéaires de $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ et $\\vert A_1\\rangle$ d'un angle de $2\\theta$.\n"
